{
  "requirement": "`habeas setup` MUST preserve existing entries in `output.html.additional-css` while adding the Habeas stylesheet at most once. It MUST report an error if `additional-css` is not an array.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Implementation.** The code is in `src/setup.rs`, in `run` (about lines 121–140), with the path helper `css_relative`.\n- If `output.html.additional-css` is absent, `run` creates an array that contains only the Habeas stylesheet path.\n- If it is an array, `run` pushes the path only when no existing entry equals it. This keeps existing entries and adds the stylesheet at most once, so repeated runs are idempotent.\n- If it is any other type, `run` returns the error `output.html.additional-css must be an array`. This happens before any file or `book.toml` write, so a failed run leaves nothing half-configured.\n- `is_configured` also checks that the stylesheet entry is present, which is consistent with the requirement.\n\n**Tests** are in `tests/setup.rs`.\n- `setup_is_repeatable` starts from a fixture whose `additional-css` is `[\"md/custom.css\"]`. It runs setup twice and asserts that `md/custom.css` is still present, that `md/habeas.css` is present, and that `md/habeas.css` appears exactly once. This covers preservation and at-most-once.\n- `setup_rejects_invalid_book_configuration` includes `additional-css = \"wrong\"`. It asserts that the command fails and that stderr contains `output.html.additional-css must be an array`. This covers the error case.\n- `setup_uses_src_when_book_table_or_source_setting_is_absent` runs setup on a book with no `additional-css`. Its `session_start` call returns an empty `SessionStart` object, which `is_configured` produces only when the stylesheet entry exists. This indirectly covers the create-from-absent path.\n\n**Gaps.** I found two minor edge cases that the requirement does not mention:\n- A differently spelled path such as `./md/habeas.css` would not be recognised as a duplicate.\n- A non-table `output` or `html` value is not handled explicitly.\n\nNeither is part of the stated requirement, and the tests cover the main design space.",
